      "title": "Approved assignment, session and access",
      "eyebrow": "Learn",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "prose",
          "text": "Permissions are made available through IAM Identity Center permission-set assignments to users or groups in specified AWS accounts. An operator needs approved access, not saved long-lived IAM user keys.",
          "role": "definition",
          "lineage": {
            "concept_ids": [
              "aws_devops.configure_secure_human_access_with_temporary_credentials"
            ],
            "teaching_block_ids": [
              "aws_devops.configure_secure_human_access_with_temporary_credentials#tb1",
              "aws_devops.configure_secure_human_access_with_temporary_credentials#tb2"
            ],
            "fact_ids": [
              "aws_devops.configure_secure_human_access_with_temporary_credentials#f1"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "type": "prose",
          "text": "Use the supplied assignment workflow to assign the approved user or group, account and permission set. Then sign in to that account and test the intended access. Keep the assignment, signed-in permission-set context and test result together: sign-in alone is not the complete access check.",
          "role": "workflow",
          "lineage": {
            "concept_ids": [
              "aws_devops.configure_secure_human_access_with_temporary_credentials"
            ],
            "teaching_block_ids": [
              "aws_devops.configure_secure_human_access_with_temporary_credentials#tb3",
              "aws_devops.configure_secure_human_access_with_temporary_credentials#tb4",
              "aws_devops.configure_secure_human_access_with_temporary_credentials#tb5"
            ],
            "fact_ids": [
              "aws_devops.configure_secure_human_access_with_temporary_credentials#f1",
              "aws_devops.configure_secure_human_access_with_temporary_credentials#f2"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "type": "prose",
          "text": "For cedar-operator in cedar-operators, compare the assigned account and permission set with the approved context. The intended test is read sandbox evidence object. Keep its expected and observed results alongside the signed-in context.",
          "role": "example",
          "lineage": {
            "concept_ids": [
              "aws_devops.configure_secure_human_access_with_temporary_credentials"
            ],
            "teaching_block_ids": [
              "aws_devops.configure_secure_human_access_with_temporary_credentials#tb4"
            ],
            "fact_ids": [
              "aws_devops.configure_secure_human_access_with_temporary_credentials#f1",
              "aws_devops.configure_secure_human_access_with_temporary_credentials#f2"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "type": "prose",
          "text": "Configure a named SSO profile with aws configure sso. Establish its session with aws sso login --profile NAME, replacing NAME with the profile name. Use this session workflow rather than storing long-lived IAM user keys.",
          "role": "mechanism",
          "lineage": {
            "concept_ids": [
              "aws_devops.configure_secure_human_access_with_temporary_credentials"
            ],
            "teaching_block_ids": [
